title: A Catalan "Yes We Can"?
view-if: podemos_surged and next_election_time - time <= 4
face-image: img/events/csqp_formation.jpg
tags: event
new-page: true
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: {!
    Q.csqp_formed = true;
    Q.parlament_current_icv = "csqp";
    Q.csqp_parlament_s = Q.icv_parlament_s;
    Q.csqp_parlament_pv = Q.icv_parlament_pv;
    Q.icv_parlament_s = 0;
    Q.icv_parlament_pv = 0;

    Q.csqp_relations = Q.icv_relations;
    Q.csqp_leader = "???";
    Q.csqp_leader_gender = "f";
    Q.csqp_ideology = "Anti-austerity left, Plurinationalism";

    for(var prov of Q.parlament_constituencies){
        for(var demo of Q.parlament_demographics){
            Q["csqp_parlament_" + prov + "_" + demo + "_support"] = Q["icv_parlament_" + prov + "_" + demo + "_support"] * 0.95;
            Q["icv_parlament_" + prov + "_" + demo + "_support"] = 0;
        }
    }


    // governing stuff
    if  (Q.president_party == "icv") {
        Q.president_party = "csqp";
    }

    if (Q.vicepresident_party == "icv") {
        Q.vicepresident_party = "csqp"
    }

    if (Q.economy_minister_party == "icv") {
        Q.economy_minister_party = "csqp";
    }

    if (Q.interior_minister_party == "icv") {
        Q.interior_minister_party = "csqp";
    }

    if (Q.health_minister_party == "icv") {
        Q.health_minister_party = "csqp";
    }

    if (Q.education_minister_party == "icv") {
        Q.education_minister_party = "csqp";
    }

    if (Q.territory_minister_party == "icv") {
        Q.territory_minister_party = "csqp";
    }

    if (Q.foreign_minister_party == "icv") {
        Q.foreign_minister_party = "csqp";
    }

    if (Q.bnl_minister_party == "icv") {
        Q.bnl_minister_party = "csqp";
    }

    if (Q.speaker_party == "icv") {
        Q.speaker_party = "csqp";
    }

    if (Q.cat_coalition.includes("icv")) {
        Q.cat_coalition = Q.cat_coalition.map(item => item === "icv" ? "csqp" : item);
        Q.cat_coalition_disp = Q.cat_coalition_disp.replaceAll("ICV-EUiA", "CSQP").replaceAll("icv", "csqp");
    }

    Q.cecp_formation_countdown = 12;
    Q.countdowns.push("cecp_formation");   
!}
role: event

= A Catalan "Yes We Can"?

With the rise of Podemos in Spain, the tide of new left parties throughout Europe, and Catalan elections right around the corner, it seems the time has come here as well. After a slow bleeding of supports and a general view of the party as outdated, ICV-EUiA has fused with new rising forces. They look to be working together with the Catalan branches of Podemos, as well as new spaces built by social movements, such as Ada Colau's BComu in Barcelona. All in all, we may be very well be witnessing a re-birth of the federal left in Catalonia. 

However, the ties between groups are fuzzy, the direction and leadership that CSQP may take are very unclear. If there's any sort of consensus figure, that is clearly in Arcadi Oliveres, an economist and long-time star of the social justice and people's rights movements in Catalonia. He's led for some time a movement demanding a "Constituent Process", a popular proceeding by which Catalans should not only decide their relationship with Spain, but also their economic system and governance.

Despite his popularity, the fact is that Arcadi Oliveres is asking for a level of control over the CSQP coalition that not many are willing to give away, and may end up blocking his proposal.

